[Term]
id: PO:0025042
name: subterranean tuber axillary vegetative bud
namespace: plant_anatomy
def: "A tuber axillary vegetative bud that is part of a subterranean tuber." [POC:curators]
comment: A structure on the tuber surface that can sprout. In potatoes, axillary vegetative buds (eyes) can determine processing quality. Scale that the breeders use to rate the buds/sprouts of tubers: 1. none, 2. swollen eye, 3. sprout ca. 1/4 inch, 4. sprout ca. 1/2 inch, 5. sprout ca. 1 inch, 6. sprout ca. 2 inch, 7. sprout ca. 3 inch, 8. new top growth, 9. chain tubers.
subset: Potato
synonym: "eye (broad)" BROAD []
synonym: "potato eye (narrow)" NARROW []
synonym: "swollen eye (narrow)" NARROW []
synonym: "tuber eye (broad)" BROAD []
