[Term]
id: PO:0025104
name: first order inflorescence axis
namespace: plant_anatomy
def: "An inflorescence axis (PO:0020122) that is the primary or main axis of an inflorescence (PO:0009049)." [NYBG:Brandon_Sinn, NYBG:Dario_Cavaliere, PO:Laurel_Cooper, POC:Ramona_Walls]
comment: Monopodial inflorescences, such as a raceme inflorescence (PO:0030115), have a centrally-located main axis; this axis is a first order inflorescence axis. In contrast, sympodial inflorescences, such as the riphidium inflorescence (PO:0030131), do not have a centrally-located main axis. The basal-most portion of a first order inflorescence axis is referred to as a peduncle (PO:0009053).
subset: Angiosperm
