[Term]
id: PO:0025323
name: flower fascicle
namespace: plant_anatomy
def: "A reproductive shoot system (PO:0025082) that is a second order inflorescence (PO:0025240), or higher, in which the inflorescence branch (PO:0009081) bears two or more flowers (PO:0009046), but is not elongated." [PMID:12644644]
comment: A fascicle appears to be a cluster of flowers in an axil of a single bract of the main inflorescence. Fascicles are common in some sections of the Fabaceae, where they are second order inflorescences.
synonym: "bundle (related)" RELATED [FNA:a5e2072c-2c55-48d8-b540-6f8aa1c0b83b]
