id: PSO:0000739
name: wheat Sclerotinia snow mold fungal disease
def: "A wheat disease caused by a Sclerotinia borealis affecting a whole plant." [AUTO:patterns/disease]
comment: Symptoms and signs: In the spring, dead leaves and plants are gray and thready. Numerous black, irregularly shaped sclerotia are usually present in and on diseased tissues.
synonym: "Snow scald" EXACT []
xref: APSNET:Wheat
is_a: PSO:0000179 ! wheat fungal disease
intersection_of: PSO:0000013 ! plant disease
intersection_of: RO:0002162 NCBITaxon:4565 ! in taxon Triticum aestivum
intersection_of: RO:0004025 PO:0000003 ! disease causes dysfunction of whole plant
intersection_of: RO:0014001 NCBITaxon:77105 ! disease has infectious agent Sclerotinia borealis
relationship: RO:0004025 PO:0000003 ! disease causes dysfunction of whole plant
relationship: RO:0014001 NCBITaxon:77105 ! disease has infectious agent Sclerotinia borealis
